# Sidekick self-hosted: shape of deploy/selfhost/ntfy.env (read by the `ntfy` service, profile `push`).
# Do NOT copy this by hand. Run `sh deploy/selfhost/ntfy-init.sh`: it generates the password hashes and the
# publish token, writes ntfy.env with mode 600 and never prints a secret. This file only documents the format.
#
# Values are in single quotes on purpose: a bcrypt hash contains "$", which Compose would otherwise interpolate.
#
# user:bcrypt-hash:role. `sidekick` gets a random password that nobody knows (it only publishes with the token);
# `phone` is the ntfy app's login. Both can only touch topics "up*" (see ntfy/server.yml).
NTFY_AUTH_USERS='sidekick:$2a$10$replace-with-bcrypt-hash:user,phone:$2a$10$replace-with-bcrypt-hash:user'
# user:token:label. The token is "tk_" and 29 more characters. The same token goes in selfhost.env as
# SIDEKICK_PUSH_AUTH_TOKEN. Rotate with `ntfy-init.sh --rotate`, then restart ntfy and the push worker.
NTFY_AUTH_TOKENS='sidekick:tk_replace-with-29-characters-xxxxx:sidekick'
